## Scenario context

Redis Sorted Sets (ZSETs) store unique members each paired with a floating-point score, kept in sorted order at all times. Internally they use a **skip list** for O(log N) range queries and a **hash table** for O(1) score lookup — giving you the best of both. The five patterns you'll reach for most: leaderboards, social feed caches, sliding-window rate limiters, priority job queues, and expiring session stores.

